The MIT License above covers the pepperscore component code, including its
Web Worker chunks in dist/assets/. It does not cover Verovio or the other
third-party components listed in dist/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.

Verovio is not compiled or bundled into pepperscore's code. pepperscore ships
two unmodified files of the Verovio 6.3.0 music engraving library
(https://www.verovio.org/, Copyright (c) Laurent Pugin and the Verovio
contributors), taken from the npm package verovio@6.3.0, with only a licence
comment added at the top of each:

  dist/verovio/verovio-module.mjs  the WebAssembly module and its glue code
  dist/verovio/verovio.mjs         the JavaScript toolkit
  dist/verovio/LICENSE             their licence notice

pepperscore's worker loads them at runtime. Verovio is licensed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version
(LGPL-3.0-or-later). Copies of the licenses are included in this package:

  LICENSES/LGPL-3.0.txt  GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3
  LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt   GNU General Public License, version 3

Corresponding source for Verovio 6.3.0:
  https://github.com/rism-digital/verovio/tree/version-6.3.0
  (git tag version-6.3.0; also published on npm as verovio@6.3.0)

Replacing Verovio: you may use a modified or different, interface-compatible
build of Verovio in place of the shipped files without rebuilding pepperscore.
Either pass the URL of a directory holding your verovio-module.mjs and
verovio.mjs (laid out like the verovio npm package's dist/ directory) as the
`verovioBaseUrl` prop of PepperScore, or replace the two files in
dist/verovio/ (or the copies your bundler emitted) with your own.
